  "description": "Design 5.5 and 5.8, A78's Back pressed twice: the keyboard is still going as the page closes. The emulator's own keyboard comes and goes as it likes, so the web view's layout is made shorter by the keyboard's height (312 px on the emulator) with DevTools' device metrics once the note has grown, and given its height back as the close begins. The list is scrolled to its end and its last card opened: closing, the app brings the card into sight above the 'keyboard', and as the view grows the list scrolls back and the card moves down by about the keyboard's height. The page must shrink onto the card where it is at each frame, with its words, and land on it.",
